The ``UID`` setter now validates the value as :rfc:`5545#section-3.8.4.7` ``text``, rejecting an empty value or one containing control characters (such as ``CR``/``LF``) that would produce an invalid calendar, by raising :exc:`~icalendar.error.InvalidCalendar`. Valid identifiers, including the common ``local@domain`` form, are accepted and never modified, so their letter casing is preserved. I used AI to assist me with this change. @Siddharth-singla
